The sky appears blue due to a phenomenon called Rayleigh scattering. When sunlight enters Earth's atmosphere, it interacts with gas molecules and small particles. Blue light has a shorter wavelength and is scattered more efficiently than other colors, making the sky look blue to our eyes.

